> API and interpretation

Nonzero period must fit the input width. Default complete-amplitude bound1048576
limits n to10; intrinsic width is at most15 to keep threshold1e-9 below the
allowed nonzero marginal probabilities. Oracle writes count only the specialized
evaluation on the known zero-output register, not a general arbitrary-state
oracle implementation. Gate calls count invocations, not primitive amplitude
operations.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

